Z||000000||artherd||12-08-2001||08:21 PM||||As promised, some shots of the shiney new wheels for the N* car!<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/northstar/2/10-rear1.jpg"> <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/northstar/2/10-rear2.jpg"> <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/northstar/2/10-rear4.jpg">  <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/northstar/2/265.jpg"> <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/northstar/2/10-rear3.jpg">  <P>I can't belive they fit!<P><BR>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">     <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red                     "Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                                        -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"<p>[This message has been edited by artherd (edited 12-08-2001).]||||reg||3
Z||000001||ejayerik||12-08-2001||08:41 PM||||They look nice. Looks like you need to lower the suspesion a bit next. Watch out for those speed-bumps.||||reg||1
Z||000002||88-DOHC||12-08-2001||08:46 PM||||I never doubted they wouldn't fit for a moment! They actually bolted on, or just set in place?<P>BTW, I told my friend about how you got the idea for the porsche rims from his web site. He was flattered.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||jimmybpei||12-08-2001||08:57 PM||||Very nice but: 18 x ?? and what is the off set<P>Do you think you could stogg a set o f 20's in there.<BR> <BR>again very nice<BR>later<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jimmybpeisig_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||88-DOHC||12-08-2001||09:02 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by jimmybpei:<BR><B>Very nice but: 18 x ?? and what is the off set<P>Do you think you could stogg a set o f 20's in there.<BR> <BR>again very nice<BR>later<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Not to take any wind away from artherd, but the rears (those shown in the picture) are 18"x10"x65mm, his fronts I believe are 18"x7.5"x55mm<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||artherd||12-08-2001||09:12 PM||||Heh, I'm not out of the woods yet!  They're just set there (like my 'calibrated wheel holder' AKA a toolbox set ontop of ann electornics bin?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>That car dosen't have any suspension in place, so I've still yet to see if I can clear the coilover strut.  But there's plenty of room still mechanically in the wheelwel, so yay!     Yes, please thank your friend profusely for me! (feel free to send him pics of what he helped start  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><BR>They're 225/40/18 on 18x7.5"-50mm offset front, 265/35/18 on 18x10"-65mm rear.   They're 'Sport Design" wheels made for Porsche 996s by BBS, and they're georgous! (and should hold the power nicely.)<P>Tyres are OE Continental ContiSport Contact.  They have two bands that are 'solid' like a slick tyre!  <P>I got the whole shebang slightly used (and at about 1/3 of retail) with '200miles' but the tyres still have the little rubber injection nibbles!  Score!<P>Best!<BR>Ben<P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 88-DOHC:<BR><B>I never doubted they wouldn't fit for a moment! They actually bolted on, or just set in place?<P>BTW, I told my friend about how you got the idea for the porsche rims from his web site. He was flattered.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000006||artherd||12-08-2001||09:28 PM||||After 18" or so, the weight of most automotive wheels starts to climb exponentially, these 2-piece 18s are actually lighter than the 15" stock alloys! (wheel and tyre combos both.)<P>Some custom 3-piece 19" and even as high as 20" wheels (eg: HRE) are *fairly* light, but also VERY expensive. <P>Also, you start having to get scary-thin sidewalls in order to fit larger wheels under a Fiero. The rear 18s above actually have (about 4mm) MORE sidewall than the 17s in my sig pic.<P>All that said, with enough time and resources, you can do *anything*  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>(HRE could make a set of 20s with a custom center and offsets to fit the stock Fiero no problem even. They'd cost nearly $2k/wheel I belive...)<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by jimmybpei:<BR><B><BR>Do you think you could stogg a set of 20's in there.<BR>again very nice<BR>later</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000007||Haze_Performance||12-08-2001||09:33 PM||||Looks GREAT!!! Cant wait to see them bolted on..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/goodlife.gif">      <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="red">1984 Indy For Sale ~ <A HREF="http://www.ClassicFiero.com" TARGET=_blank>Click Here</A> </FONT></FONT>||||reg||14
Z||000008||Nashco||12-08-2001||10:36 PM||||Looks sweet man! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  That is a LOT of tire back there, ought to hook up awesome!  Hmm...I can totally see that thing lowered about four or five inches with some fender flares...after you get the N* in and running, of course <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Keep at it man, you are on track to build one of the baddest Fieros (and cars for that matter) around!<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000009||88-DOHC||12-09-2001||02:00 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by artherd:<BR><B>That car dosen't have any suspension in place, so I've still yet to see if I can clear the coilover strut.  But there's plenty of room still mechanically in the wheelwel, so yay!     Yes, please thank your friend profusely for me! (feel free to send him pics of what he helped start    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well, its good you got 18", because if you had gotten 17" in that width they wouldn't have fit (at least thats what my friend told me, when I told him what you were doing). Apperently with the boxster rims, they come rather close to some bolt on the rear suspension (I think the top strut bolt).  <P>The other thing, is there is no way you would have been able to find wheels like that if you had stuck with the 5-100 bolt pattern (not without going to a complete custom wheel shop). <p>[This message has been edited by 88-DOHC (edited 12-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||artherd||12-09-2001||03:33 AM||||Yep, and yep!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>996s also came with 17" wheels/tyres, no way they'd have fit in back!  <P>Yeah, they're pretty nice light and strong 2-piece wheels, and can be had cheap!<P>The 5x130 bolt conversion is a pain, but man is it all gonna be strong when it's done!<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 88-DOHC:<BR><B>  Well, its good you got 18", because if you had gotten 17" in that width they wouldn't have fit (at least thats what my friend told me, when I told him what you were doing). Apperently with the boxster rims, they come rather close to some bolt on the rear suspension (I think the top strut bolt).  <P>The other thing, is there is no way you would have been able to find wheels like that if you had stuck with the 5-100 bolt pattern (not without going to a complete custom wheel shop). <P>[This message has been edited by 88-DOHC (edited 12-09-2001).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000011||Screwie||12-09-2001||04:13 AM||||Looks absolutely great, artherd! Now get that thing on the road with your N* and make some vids  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
